I wouldn't recommend reverse genociding giant beetles.  From one of my
favorite spoily pages, "Eating Corpses For Food And Intrinsics"
<http://www.geocities.com/dcorbett42/nethack/corpse.htm>, giant beetles
are poisonous to eat, and only have a 33% chance of giving poison
resistance.  One way you could be guaranteed of getting poison
resistance would be to use your magic lamp wish for a blessed tin of
green dragon meat.  If you don't want to use your wish, there're several
species I would consider better candidates for rev-geno than giant
beetles, like black puddings, most of the nagas & naga hatchlings, and
others.  The best option might be to rev-geno nurses, as eating a nurse
corpse has a 73% chance of giving poison resistance, and you can dance
w/ the nurses for extra hp (but if you dance too much, you won't get
their corpse to eat).

I'm not 100% positive, but I don't think you can rev-geno or otherwise
create species that have been genocided.  There are some ways that you
can create extinct species (120 or more have appeared in the game), but
IIRC any species that has been genocided will NEVER appear.

